  "family": "FAMILY03",
  "mapping_id": "MAP_F03_A",
  "evidence_basis": [
    {
      "evidence_id": "F03_M0_ACTIONS",
      "source_type": "M0",
      "source_path": "ignition/reports/evaluations/ignition-220-cognitive-evolution-r0/families/FAMILY03/m0.md",
      "source_sha256": "691b63e6ff4324acc23a09a35114df3fbb75668d39de3d8283386f30b110331a",
      "locator": {
        "start_line": 14,
        "end_line": 17,
        "excerpt_sha256": "fcbb70c67e63a6f56a7f75a1e6e6d94ce3ebf9927198dc8195b03a2f6e47cb1e"
      },
      "display_excerpt": "- SCREEN_PASS: record the screened lot as within M0's temperature criterion.\n- STABILITY_REVIEW: quarantine the screening decision for an independent stability review.\n- RECONCILE_LOGGER: recover logger clock, missing intervals, or custody mismatch before classification.\n- UNSCORABLE: do not classify if required temperature, product identity, or logger provenance is unavailable.\n",
      "supports": "Names the frozen M0 screening, review, logger-reconciliation, and unscorable actions kept available.",
      "claim_type": "method_rule"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "F03_M0_PROCEDURE",
      "source_type": "M0",
      "source_path": "ignition/reports/evaluations/ignition-220-cognitive-evolution-r0/families/FAMILY03/m0.md",
      "source_sha256": "691b63e6ff4324acc23a09a35114df3fbb75668d39de3d8283386f30b110331a",
      "locator": {
        "start_line": 21,
        "end_line": 24,
        "excerpt_sha256": "92c79d0332999f6080c51782f31263f6f27446e064db7dea6442724da864d205"
      },
      "display_excerpt": "1. Confirm logger calibration, clock alignment, shipment identity, 15-minute sampling interval, and completeness across the defined shipment window.\n2. Compute the arithmetic mean of the valid 15-minute readings for each eight-hour segment and the shipment-wide mean.\n3. If any eight-hour segment mean or the shipment-wide mean is above 8.0 °C, select STABILITY_REVIEW. If required samples are missing or custody/clock checks fail, select RECONCILE_LOGGER; unresolved required inputs yield UNSCORABLE.\n4. Otherwise select SCREEN_PASS. A screen pass is a triage result under M0; it is not an unconditional product-safety guarantee.\n",
      "supports": "Defines M0 logger completeness, interval means, and review routing; used only as baseline and stop context.",
      "claim_type": "method_rule"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "F03_E1_PULSED_P",
      "source_type": "E1",
      "source_path": "ignition/reports/evaluations/ignition-220-cognitive-evolution-r0/families/FAMILY03/revision-evidence-e1.md",
      "source_sha256": "fba2eef834fa1ae9b43665ecbaa15a2bf8690f840cc0a56483701a8e7601c5ff",
      "locator": {
        "start_line": 16,
        "end_line": 18,
        "excerpt_sha256": "2c45b96e1efd4c8da249499054969771babc46571017a542d4fb5628eab77373"
      },
      "display_excerpt": "| OBS-01 | group P; warm dock handoff trace | 6.1 °C | 14.2 °C | 11 min | 88.4% | 88.1 / 88.7% |\n| OBS-02 | group P; repeated route and unit | 6.3 °C | 13.7 °C | 9 min | 90.1% | 89.8 / 90.4% |\n| OBS-03 | group P; second unit, separate shipment | 6.0 °C | 14.4 °C | 13 min | 85.9% | 85.4 / 86.4% |\n",
      "supports": "Three group-P observations show brief high-rate pulses with assay results below the stated reference while 15-minute means remain within M0.",
      "claim_type": "observed"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "F03_E1_CONTRAST",
      "source_type": "E1",
      "source_path": "ignition/reports/evaluations/ignition-220-cognitive-evolution-r0/families/FAMILY03/revision-evidence-e1.md",
      "source_sha256": "fba2eef834fa1ae9b43665ecbaa15a2bf8690f840cc0a56483701a8e7601c5ff",
      "locator": {
        "start_line": 19,
        "end_line": 20,
        "excerpt_sha256": "27116db57bebfaae9d62de74e7d25b48620283da5fbe7de49ac5b936150cb6eb"
      },
      "display_excerpt": "| OBS-04 | group S; matched 15-minute mean, brief dock pulse | 6.2 °C | 14.0 °C | 10 min | 98.7% | 98.3 / 99.1% |\n| OBS-05 | group P; no observed pulse, continuous profile | 6.5 °C | 7.1 °C | 0 min | 99.0% | 98.6 / 99.4% |\n",
      "supports": "The group-S pulse contrast and group-P continuous profile bound interpretation of the group-P observations.",
      "claim_type": "observed"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "F03_E1_LIMITS",
      "source_type": "E1",
      "source_path": "ignition/reports/evaluations/ignition-220-cognitive-evolution-r0/families/FAMILY03/revision-evidence-e1.md",
      "source_sha256": "fba2eef834fa1ae9b43665ecbaa15a2bf8690f840cc0a56483701a8e7601c5ff",
      "locator": {
        "start_line": 27,
        "end_line": 29,
        "excerpt_sha256": "e2e47e6dfb0c9bd01090180433980ca4a5816e6e7f9ca963c4adc7a78ffdeffd"
      },
      "display_excerpt": "The source rows establish a reproducible contradiction to mean-only screening for the observed group-P pulse cases while retaining a stable continuous-profile group-P case and a pulsed group-S case. The group and detailed exposure are independently recorded and not inferred from the assay. The records do not support treating every isolated high sample as a confirmed degradation event, and OBS-06 does not identify whether a pulse occurred. The pulse amplitudes/durations observed here do not establish a universal threshold for every formulation or logger cadence.\n\nA tempting but unsupported overreaction is to classify any one-minute reading above 8 °C as a confirmed product failure or to discard all logger-based screening. M0's calibration, custody, continuous-profile behavior, and the product-specific contrast remain separately observable.\n",
      "supports": "The observations do not establish a universal pulse threshold or confirmed degradation from any isolated high reading.",
      "claim_type": "method_rule"
    }
  ],
